# The other credential file. Already excluded from the Docker and Cloud Build contexts, but it
# was never excluded from git — and some SDKs (manim-voiceover's ElevenLabs backend among them)
# create one on import, so a real key can appear here without anyone deciding to put it there.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Persisted platform OAuth credentials (per-client token dirs)
.platform_credentials/

# Claude
claude.md
.claude
screenshot_review/

# Node deps (screenshot tooling etc.) — installed, not committed
node_modules/
testing_files/experiment_report.md
testing_files/experiment_report.html
testing_files/experiment_results/
testing_files/experiment_archive/
testing_files/benchmark_history.jsonl
testing_files/auction_cash_runs/

# Manim build products: one clip per animation plus the LaTeX step's output. Large,
# numerous, and regenerated by a re-render -- the finished videos beside them are kept.
visualizations/render_cache/**/partial_movie_files/
# Renders of every quality. The finished -qh videos are PUBLISHED by copying them into
# docs/videos/, which is where MkDocs can serve them and where the tracked copy lives -- so
# tracking them here as well would put the same 74MB into the history twice.
visualizations/render_cache/videos/
# Stills, which are what Manim writes when a scene plays no animations -- always a mistake
# in this directory rather than a deliverable.
visualizations/render_cache/images/
# Synthesised narration audio: regenerated from the NARRATION block in each scene, and
# re-synthesised whenever a line changes. Cached only to keep re-renders offline.
visualizations/render_cache/voiceovers/
visualizations/render_cache/Tex/
visualizations/render_cache/texts/

# The rendered explainer videos and their posters in docs/videos/ ARE tracked: the docs are published by
# .github/workflows/docs.yml from a fresh checkout, so a video that is not in git is not on the published site (they
# were untracked from 2026-09-23, and every automated publish from 2026-10-15 went out without them). Publishing a
# re-render: copy it into docs/videos/ with `ffmpeg -movflags +faststart` (manim writes the moov atom last, which stops
# a browser seeking a streamed file) and commit it.

# The built copy of docs/videos. `mkdocs build` re-copies docs/videos into site/ every time, so tracking it would
# commit the same binaries twice.
site/videos/

# Circular headshots built by visualizations/shared/prepare_season_data.py from the app's
# .cache/headshots. Build output: 161 PNGs that dominate any diff of this branch. Rebuilding
# them needs the app run once against the season so the cache fills from cdn.nba.com -- so
# unlike the scenes, the inputs are NOT all in the repo. Accepted deliberately: if that source
# ever stops serving them the headshots need a new source regardless of what git holds.
visualizations/prepared_assets/
